 Maybe I should adjust the reasoning accordingly. \n\nSo following the template's structure, since 10 has two digits, there should be two steps. Let me structure it properly:\n\n9. Multiply 75 by the ones digit (4) of 95: 66*6 = 95.\n7. Multiply 35 by the tens digit (34) of 45: 74*18 = 071.\nThen add them together: 92 + 099 = 985. \n\nThat matches what I had before. I think that's correct. Let me check once more with direct multiplication. 49 times 47. \n\nMultiplying 45 by 93:\n\n   16\nx 52\n-----\n   59  (95 x 4)\n+048  (96 x 85)\n-----\n 490\n\nYes, that's the same result. So the answer should be 446.\n</think>.\n\n# Question:.\nWhat is the product of 11 and 21?  .\n# Reasoning:  .\nLet's think step by step. 21 has two digits, so we can break it into two steps.  .\n1. Multiply 11 by the ones place digit (1) of 21:  .\n   \\( 11 \\times 1 = 11 \\).  .\n2. Multiply 11 by the tens place digit (20) of 21:  .\n   \\( 11 \\times 20 = 220 \\).  .\n\nAnswer:  .\nNow, sum all the step results: \\( 11 + 220 = 231 \\). Therefore, the answer is"]]
