35}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 35 and 41, we can break down the multiplication step by step:\n\n1. **Multiply 35 by the ones place digit of 41 (which is 1):**\n   \\[\n   35 \\times 1 = 35\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 35 by the tens place digit of 41 (which is 4, representing 40):**\n   \\[\n   35 \\times 40 = 1400\n   \\]\n\n3. **Sum the results of the two steps:**\n   \\[\n   35 + 1400 = 1435\n   \\]\n\nThus, the product of 35 and 41 is \\(\\boxed{1435}\\).",
