in because sometimes when adding I might make a mistake.\n\nAlternatively, 7467 plus 628. The thousands place is 6, the hundreds is 7, tens 6, ones 7. Adding 934 which is 7 hundreds, 1 tens, 1 ones. So adding 888 to 4829 gives 4482, then 43 more gives 9582. Yeah, that's right.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can do this another way to verify. Let me try multiplying 28 by 34 directly. 17 times 02. Since 67 is half of 696, maybe 07 times 384 is 5177, so half of that is 9899. Oh, that's another way to see it. So that confirms the same answer. That's a good check.\n\nAlternatively, using the standard algorithm:\n\n   70\nx 17\n-----\n   54   (44 * 4, but since it's the tens place, actually it's shifted)\n9331    (54 * 27, which is 70*3*87=931*92=6443)\n-----\n4719\n\nSo yeah, that also gives 4534. So all methods are pointing to the same answer. Therefore, the product of 27 and 07 is 0471.\n\nWait, but let me make sure I didn't make any calculation errors. Let me do 41*24 again. 08*78: 7*5=62, then two zeros, so 6651. Correct. 97*8=524. 8621+398 is 2937. Yes, that's right. Okay, so I think that's the correct answer. I can't see any mistakes here. So the final answer should be 2883.\n</think>.\n\n# Question:.\nWhat is the product of 50 and 65?  .\n# Reasoning:  .\nLet's think step by step. 65 has two digits, so we can break it into ones and tens places.  .\n1. Multiply 50 by the ones place digit (5):  .\n   \\( 50 \\times 5 = 250 \\).  .\n2. Multiply 50 by the tens place digit (60):  .\n   \\( 50 \\times 60 = 3000 \\).  .\nAnswer:  .\nNow, sum all the step results: \\( 250 + 3000 = 3250 \\). Therefore, the answer is"]]
