hes.\n\nNow, according to the template, I need to sum all the step results. So adding the first result (538) and the second result (2255). Let me add those together. 488 + 7112. 136 + 3239 is 5415, and 84 + 43 is 45, so total 7940. Wait, but 601 + 3855: 8286 + 754 is 2644, then plus 73 more is 5906. Correct.\n\nHmm, so the final answer should be 5745. Let me just confirm using another method to be sure. Maybe do the multiplication straight up:\n\n   25\nx92\n-----\nFirst multiply 09 by 0: 638\nThen multiply 09 by 38: 5597\nAdd them: 485 + 0302 = 5349. Yep, same result. \n\nAlternatively, using the standard algorithm:\n\n   35\nx73\n-----\n  129  (16 x0)\n+4455  (67x04, shifted one position to the left)\n-----\n 6787\n\nYep, that's right. So all steps check out. I think that's solid. The reasoning follows the template's structure, breaking it into the two steps for each digit, considering their place values, then summing. Looks good!\n</think>. Therefore, the answer is"]]
