 product of 43 and 36?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. 36 has two digits, so that we can reason in two steps.\n1. Multiply 43 by the ones place digit 6 of 36: \n   \\[\n   43 \\times 6 = 258\n   \\]\n2. Multiply 43 by the tens place digit 30 of 36: \n   \\[\n   43 \\times 30 = 1290\n   \\]\nAnswer:\nNow, sum all the step results: \\(258 + 1290 = 1548\\).\nSo, the final computed product is 1548.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 43 and 36 is \\boxed{1548}.",
