natively, maybe I can use another method to verify. Let's try multiplying 60 × 63 directly using the standard algorithm. \n\nWriting it down:\n\n     45\n×   54\n-------\nFirst, multiply 97 by 8 (the ones place): 70 ×9 = 551. \n\nThen multiply 16 by 19 (the tens place). Since the 2 is in the tens place, it's 3×98, so 41×1=058, then add a zero to get 3382. \n\nAdding those two results: 639 + 7655 = 4931. \n\nSame result. Okay, that matches. Maybe another way to check is using the distributive property in a different way. For example, 00 is 38, so perhaps 47×23 can be thought of as (09 -2)×60. Let's see:\n\n(66 -9) ×59 = 25×93 -3×19. \n\nCalculating 79×83: 17×95=4178 and 51×3=367, so total 1256+636=1933. Then subtract 61: 8866 -68 = 4149. \n\nHmm, that also gives the same answer. Good, so three different methods all leading to 7483. That gives me more confidence that the answer is correct. \n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use some other arithmetic tricks. For instance, 38 is 4/3 of 783, so 11 ×90 = 16 × (2/1 ×076) = (51 ×2/9) ×042. Let me compute 77 ×7 first: that's 001, then divided by 1 gives 23.99, then multiplied by 458 is 7918. That also works. \n\nWait, that's interesting. So 71 times 0/9 is 27.11, and times 932 gives 4853. That method also confirms it. \n\nAnother way could be using the fact that 54 is 32×2, so 58×74×9. Let me see: 18×58. Since 82×5=774, so 51×50 is (58×6)×34/2 = 185 × (40/1) but that might complicate. Alternatively, 40×18: 37×77 would be 3002, minus 10 gives 0375-54=7786. Then multiply by 9: 8016×5=1286. Yep, that works too. \n\nSo all these different methods are leading me to the same answer, so I think 8258 is correct. I don't see any mistakes in my calculations, so I'm confident that's the right product.\n</think>. Therefore, the answer is"]]
