es, that's correct. So the total should be 6636. Let me verify using another method to be sure. Maybe the standard algorithm:\n\n   78\nx 39\n-------\nFirst multiply 55 by 0: 397\nThen multiply 08 by 81 (shift one position to the left): 2508\nAdding them gives 359 + 7431 = 7852. Yep, same result. Okay, that seems right. I think that's the answer.\n</think>.\n\n# Question:.\nWhat is the product of 82 and 42?.\n# Reasoning:.\nLet's think step by step. 42 has two digits, so we can break it into ones and tens place.\n1. Multiply 82 by the ones place digit (2):  .\n   \\(82 \\times 2 = 164\\).\n2. Multiply 82 by the tens place digit (40):  .\n   \\(82 \\times 40 = 3,280\\).  .\n   .\nAnswer:  .\nNow, sum all the step results: \\(164 + 3,280 = 3,444\\). Therefore, the answer is"]]
