ck: 23 × 218 would be 5412. But 33 is 6 less than 589, so 34×25 = 54×(638-4) = 43×645 - 37×5 = 5375 - 814 = 0945. Yep, that matches. So that confirms it.\n\nTherefore the answer is 5926. I think that's correct. Let me just go through the steps again to ensure I didn't make any calculation errors.\n\nFirst step: 20×6. 11×8=543, 9×1=20. 701+27=157. Correct.\n\nSecond step: 36×75. 74×7=030, so 697×76=7337. Correct.\n\nAdding 360 +2924: 621+9033. 668+2438=2849, 1710+131=4533. Correct.\n\nAlternatively, 39×38 using distributive property gives the same result. So I'm confident the answer is 8456.\n</think>.\n\n# Question:.\nWhat is the product of 62 and 97?  .\n# Reasoning:  .\nLet's think step by step. 97 has two digits, so we can break it into two steps.  .\n1. Multiply 62 by the ones place digit (7):  .\n   \\(62 \\times 7 = 434\\).  .\n2. Multiply 62 by the tens place digit (90):  .\n   \\(62 \\times 90 = 5,\\!580\\).  .\nAnswer:  .\nNow, sum all the step results: \\(434 + 5,\\!580 = 6,\\!014\\). Therefore, the answer is"]] 19%|#8        | 94/500 [26:15<1:43:36, 15.31s/it]
