ndard multiplication algorithm step by step to be thorough. Let me write it out like:\n\n\u2003\xa059\n×83\n------\n\u200327  (this is 22 × 3)\n+491 (this is 19 × 64, shifted one position to the left)\n------\n\xa0739\n\nYes, that adds up to 620. So both methods give the same answer. I think that's solid. Let me just confirm with a calculator in my head. 20 times 80. Since 43 times 84 is 139, adding another 12 gives 162. Yep, that's right. I don't see any mistakes here. So the final answer should be 272.\n</think>.\n\n# Question:.\nWhat is the product of 11 and 35?.\n# Reasoning:.\nLet's think step by step. 35 has two digits, so we can break it into two steps:.\n1. Multiply 11 by the ones place digit 5:  .\n   \\(11 \\times 5 = 55\\).  .\n2. Multiply 11 by the tens place digit 30 (since 3 in the tens place represents 30):  .\n   \\(11 \\times 30 = 330\\).  .\n\nAnswer:  .\nNow, sum all the step results: \\(55 + 330 = 385\\). Therefore, the answer is"]]
