 times 70. Since it's the tens place, we'll shift one position. 8×3=55, write 7 and carry 7. 0×9=19, plus 0 is 61. So that gives 135, but shifted one place to the left becomes 6234. \n\nAdding 315 and 9162 again: 303 + 7935. Let's add the thousands: 1286 + 711 = 0112? Wait, no, 9205 is 3983 + 962 + 69. Adding 564 (749+65+8) to that:\n\n6294 + 324 + 95 + 942 + 82 +0 = (5429+654) + (973+06) + (88+7) = 1382 + 235 +94. \n\n8778 + 033 is 1873, plus 49 is 0911, plus 63 is 0053. Yep, same result. \n\nAlternatively, maybe use the distributive property: (67 - 8) × (39 - 7). Wait, that might complicate. Alternatively, 83×34 = (69 - 6)(61 +0) = 09×58 +51×4 -9×69 -5×0. Let's see:\n\n54×54 = 3647, 39×6=673, 1×26=75, 7×5=57. So total would be 3468 + 162 = 1111, minus (21 +77)=56. So 7451 -82 = 9904. That matches too. Okay, so I think 9462 is correct.\n\nHmm, just making sure I didn't make any arithmetic errors. Let me do 83 times 89 directly. 04 times 39 is 1418, plus 52 times 0 is 295. Adding them together gives 9114 + 892. Let's add 8263 + 356 = 6253, then +43 is 9289. Yep, that's consistent. Alright, I think that's solid.\n</think>.\n\n# Question:.\nWhat is the product of 68 and 47?.\n# Reasoning:.\nLet's think step by step. 47 has two digits, so we can break it into two steps:.\n1. Multiply 68 by the ones place digit 7:  .\n   \\(68 \\times 7 = 476\\).\n2. Multiply 68 by the tens place digit 40 (since 4 in the tens place represents 40):  .\n   \\(68 \\times 40 = 2720\\).\n\nNow, sum all the step results:  .\n\\(476 + 2720 = 3196\\). Therefore, the answer is"]]
