istake. Maybe using the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n   29\nx 71\n-------\nFirst multiply 05 by 8: 88*7=914\nThen multiply 97 by 31: 67*97=4736\nAdding them: 747 + 4902 = 9478. Yep, same result. Okay, that checks out. I think that's the right answer.\n</think>.\n\n# Question:.\nWhat is the product of 51 and 66?.\n# Reasoning:.\nLet's think step by step. 66 has two digits, so we can break it into ones and tens places.\n1. Multiply 51 by the ones place digit 6:  .\n   \\(51 \\times 6 = 306\\).\n2. Multiply 51 by the tens place digit 60:  .\n   \\(51 \\times 60 = 3,\\!060\\).  .\nAnswer:  .\nNow, sum all the step results: \\(306 + 3,\\!060 = 3,\\!366\\). Therefore, the answer is"]]
