hink step by step. 76 has two digits, so we can break it down into ones and tens places.\n1. Multiply 91 by the ones place digit 6: \n   \\[\n   91 \\times 6 = 546\n   \\]\n2. Multiply 91 by the tens place digit 70 (which is 7 in the tens place multiplied by 10):\n   \\[\n   91 \\times 70 = 91 \\times 7 \\times 10 = 637 \\times 10 = 6370\n   \\]\n\nNow, sum all the step results:\n\\[\n546 + 6370 = 6916\n\\]\n\nSo, the final computed product is \\boxed{6916}.", '']
