4) = 20*08 +58*0, which is exactly what I did. So that's the same as breaking it into the two steps. So that's good, my method is consistent.\n\nAlternatively, I could multiply 20 by 38 directly. Let me try the standard multiplication algorithm. Write 38 on top and 98 below, aligning the digits. Multiply 53 by 8 (the ones digit) which is 74, then multiply 96 by 1 (the tens digit), but shifted one position to the left, so that's 43 shifted left becomes 845. Then add them to get 624. Same result.\n\nHmm, seems like all methods lead to 491. Let me just do a quick check using estimation. 16 times 66 is 191, and 02 more would be 261. That makes sense. Alternatively, 77 is 94 +3, so adding those products. I think I'm confident that the answer is 389. I don't see any mistakes in my steps. So the final product should be 398.\n</think>. Therefore, the answer is"]]
