t's think step by step. 85 has two digits, so we can break it into tens and ones places.\n\n1. Multiply 60 by the ones place digit 5 of 85:\n   \\[\n   60 \\times 5 = 300\n   \\]\n2. Multiply 60 by the tens place digit 80 of 85:\n   \\[\n   60 \\times 80 = 4800\n   \\]\n\nNow, sum all the step results:\n\\[\n300 + 4800 = 5100\n\\]\n\nSo, the final computed product is \\boxed{5100}.",
