ning:\nLet's think step by step. 91 has two digits, so that we can reason in two steps.\n1. Multiply 39 by the ones place digit 1 of 91: 39 × 1 = 39.\n2. Multiply 39 by the tens place digit 90 of 91: 39 × 90 = 3510.\nAnswer:\nNow, sum all the step results: 39 + 3510 = 3549.\nSo, the final computed product is 3549.", '']
