erly without the confusion in the initial thought process. \n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 31 and 69 is \\boxed{2139}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 31 and 69, we can break down the multiplication into simpler steps by using the distributive property.\n\n1. Multiply 31 by the ones place digit of 69 (which is 9):\n   \\[\n   31 \\times 9 = 279\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 31 by the tens place digit of 69 (which is 60):\n   \\[\n   31 \\times 60 = 1860\n   \\]\n\n3. Add the results of the two steps together:\n   \\[\n   279 + 1860 = 2139\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the final computed product is \\(\\boxed{2139}\\).",
