 by the ones place digit (3):**\n   \\[\n   97 \\times 3 = 291\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 97 by the tens place digit (80):**\n   \\[\n   97 \\times 80 = 97 \\times 8 \\times 10 = 776 \\times 10 = 7760\n   \\]\n\n3. **Sum the results of the two steps:**\n   \\[\n   291 + 7760 = 8051\n   \\]\n\nThus, the product of 97 and 83 is \\(\\boxed{8051}\\).",
