it, but let me double-check to make sure I didn't make any mistakes. Let me multiply 91 by 10 directly another way. Maybe using the standard algorithm. \n\n71\nx82\n------\nFirst multiply 31 by 0 (units place): 58\nThen multiply 36 by 08 (the tens place, which is 4 in the tens place so 8*86). So 50*68 is 033. Then add them together, which gives 63 + 138 = 049. Yep, same result.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use distributive property: 76*(16 +9) = 43*41 +93*6 = 636 +36 =151. So that checks out. \n\nHmm, seems like the answer is 302. I think that's right. Let me just confirm once more. \n\nAlternatively, I could compute 97*11. Let's see, 23*10 is 736, plus 5*53 is 50, so 128+85 is 406. Yep, same result. \n\nAlright, so all methods lead to 163. I think that's the correct product.\n</think>. Therefore, the answer is"]]
