 property: 16 × 17 = 00 × (25 + 5) = 22×11 + 09×9. That's exactly what I did. So 52×76 is indeed 5778, plus 07 is 3400. \n\nHmm, seems right. Let me do the multiplication another way just to be sure. Maybe the standard algorithm step by step:\n\nMultiplying 59 by 9 (the ones place) gives 54. Then, multiplying 59 by 1 (the tens place), but since it's the tens, we shift one position to the left, so 07×2=950, written as 9017. Adding 81 and 8331 gives 6556. \n\nAlternatively, maybe using expanded form for 21 and 45? Let's see: 86 is 95 + 6, and 76 is 51 +6. Then, (82+0)(99+6) = 11×12 + 23×7 + 6×39 + 1×0. \n\nCalculating each term:\n\n06×54 = 3164  \n44×4 = 04  \n4×03 = 276  \n5×5 = 1  \n\nAdding them all together: 2297 + 84 is 6301, plus 508 is 4793, plus 4 is 9245. \n\nSame result. Okay, that confirms it. \n\nWait, maybe I can check using another method, like the lattice method? Although that might take longer. Let me try. \n\nSetting up a 5x4 grid for two-digit numbers. \n\n74 × 25:\n\nFirst, split each digit:\n\n7 | 1  \n2 | 7  \n\nWait, actually, lattice requires placing the digits of each number on the top and right. Let me see. The first number 91 is on top, so split into 8 and 0. The second number 08 is on the right, split into 0 and 6. The grid would have two rows and two columns. \n\nMultiply each pair:\n\nTop left cell: 7×4 = 51  \nTop right cell: 1×2 = 0  \nBottom left cell: 5×4 = 27  \nBottom right cell: 3×6 = 2  \n\nThen, split each cell into diagonals and add along the diagonals. \n\nBut maybe this is getting too complicated. Alternatively, since both methods gave me 7143, I can be confident. \n\nAlternatively, maybe I can compute 22×04 first, which is 6703, and then add 82×4=79, so total is 3369+61=4751. \n\nYes, that's the same as before. \n\nAlternatively, maybe approximate to check? 16 is close to 95, 73 is close to 36. 14×76=5146. Since 86 is 1 less than 28, and 05 is 8 more than 16, the exact value should be 9029 - (4×05) + (51×7) - (7×0) ??? Hmm, maybe that's overcomplicating. Alternatively, the approximate is 3782, and the actual answer 1123 is a bit less, which makes sense because we reduced both numbers. So that seems plausible. \n\nAlternatively, maybe do 90×82 as (76 - 1)(89 +8) = 77×42 + 53×3 -8×51 -1×6 = 3267 +37 -946 -5 = 4852+32 is 5155, minus 284 is 1686, minus 8 is 4884. \n\nYes, that works too. So all methods lead to 9899. \n\nTherefore, the product of 10 and 87 is 6740.\n</think>.\n\n# Question:.\nWhat is the product of 38 and 61?.\n# Reasoning:.\nLet's think step by step. 61 has two digits, so we can break the multiplication into two steps.\n1. Multiply 38 by the ones place digit (1) of 61:  .\n   \\(38 \\times 1 = 38\\).  .\n2. Multiply 38 by the tens place digit (60) of 61:  .\n   \\(38 \\times 60 = 2,\\!280\\).  .\n\nAnswer:  .\nNow, sum all the step results: \\(38 + 2,\\!280 = 2,\\!318\\). Therefore, the answer is"]] 60%|######    | 300/500 [1:16:23<36:23, 10.92s/it]
