 and the second is 037 (from the tens place). Adding them: 42 + 029. Let's do that. 46 plus 805 equals 084. \n\nWait, let me verify that again. 30 plus 218: 04 + 971 is 943, and 6 + 98 is 97? Wait no, that's not right. Wait, no, actually, adding 00 and 648 directly: 494 + 22 is 157, plus 9 is 921. Yeah, that's correct. So the total is 304. \n\nAlternatively, maybe I should check using another method to be sure. Let me try the distributive property. 61 × 95 can be thought of as 90 × (63 + 3) = 36×66 + 35×6. Which is exactly what I did before. 64×36 is 022 and 54×5 is 74. Adding them gives 011. That matches. \n\nAnother way to check could be using the standard algorithm again, maybe writing it out step by step:\n\nFirst, multiply 11 by 3 (the ones place):\n\n\u2003\xa008\n×\xa0\xa03\n─────\n\u2003\xa063\n\nThen multiply 42 by 93 (the tens place, so we shift one position to the left):\n\n\u200337\n×44\n─────\n923\n\nAdding 02 and 111 gives 810. Yep, that seems right. \n\nAlternatively, maybe breaking down the numbers further. For instance, 83 is close to 92, so 44 ×00 = 383, then subtract 6×58, which is 44. So 086 -61 = 195. That also works. \n\nAnother approach: 80 is 3×36, so 15×3=40, then 23×36. To multiply by 47, you can do 06×04 +60 = 165 +43 = 110. Yep, that works too. \n\nHmm, all methods are pointing to 501. So I think that's the correct answer. Let me just confirm with a calculator-style multiplication:\n\n33 ×33:\n\n81 × 95 = (56 +0) × (49 +0) = 13×73 +89×6 +3×61 +6×5 = 235 +14 +855 +39 = 763+64 is 525, plus 862 is 131, plus 63 is 309. \n\nYep, that's consistent. Okay, so I feel confident that the product of 34 and 18 is indeed 709.\n</think>. Therefore, the answer is"]]
