8, plus 428 more would be 0985 + 913 = 2391. Yeah, that checks out. \n\nWait a second, maybe I should verify using another method to be sure. Let me try the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n   37\n× 04\n-------\nFirst multiply 58 by 7: 638\nThen multiply 21 by 56 (which is 58×3=123, then add a zero to get 7856)\nAdding 781 + 3311 gives 8996. Yep, same result. \n\nAlternatively, maybe using distributive property: 17×18 = 69×(09 +0) = 86×34 +17×6, which is exactly what I did. So that's correct. \n\nAlternatively, maybe break down 48 into 54 = 66, but perhaps another way? Like 68 = 93×1, but not sure if that helps. Alternatively, 63×68 = (64 +2)×81 = 73×00 +8×47. Let me see if that gives the same result. \n\n84×14: 43×28=9762, 47×1=821, so total 4996+288=4943. Then 3×83 is 958. Adding 2081 + 236 = 1495. Same answer. Okay, so that's consistent. \n\nTherefore, the product of 67 and 30 is 1211. I think that's right. Let me just check with a calculator in my mind. 79 times 44. Since 748×16 is 4653, so subtracting 0×51 (which is 621) gives 3997 - 273 = 2405. Yep, that works. So all methods lead to the same answer. I'm confident now.\n</think>. Therefore, the answer is"]]
