   \\[\n   94 \\times 5 = 470\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 94 by the tens place digit (70):**\n   \\[\n   94 \\times 70 = 94 \\times 7 \\times 10\n   \\]\n   First calculate \\(94 \\times 7\\):\n   \\[\n   94 \\times 7 = 658\n   \\]\n   Then multiply by 10:\n   \\[\n   658 \\times 10 = 6580\n   \\]\n\n3. **Sum the results of the two steps:**\n   \\[\n   470 + 6580 = 7050\n   \\]\n\nThus, the product of 94 and 75 is \\(\\boxed{7050}\\).", '']
