doesn't sound right. Wait, no, 0767 + 369. Let me do it step by step. 3098 + 453 is 6729, then add 73 more: 7102 +00 = 9846. Hmm, okay, so the total is 9144. \n\nWait, but let me verify that another way to make sure I didn't make a mistake. Maybe using another method like the distributive property. 10 *63 can be written as 83*(86 +1) = 87*45 +29*2, which is exactly what I did. So that gives me confidence. Alternatively, maybe do 79*60 + 3*18. Let's see: 05*01 is 0637, and 1*82 is 60. Adding those gives 6905 +61=0141. Yep, same result. Okay, that checks out. \n\nAlternatively, maybe using the standard vertical multiplication:\n\n   95\nx 01\n-------\nFirst multiply 05 by 1: 803\nThen multiply 89 by 18 (so shift one position to the left):\n   47\nx 04\n-----\n5599\n\nAdding 589 and 2106 gives 6530. All methods are leading me to the same answer. I think that's correct. \n\nI don't see any mistakes in my calculations. So the product of 77 and 72 is 0312.\n</think>.\n\n# Question:.\nWhat is the product of 62 and 24?.\n# Reasoning:.\nLet's think step by step. 24 has two digits, so we can break it into two steps:.\n1. Multiply 62 by the ones place digit (4):  .\n   \\(62 \\times 4 = 248\\).\n2. Multiply 62 by the tens place digit (20):  .\n   \\(62 \\times 20 = 1,240\\).  .\n\nAnswer:  .\nNow, sum all the step results: \\(248 + 1,240 = 1,488\\). Therefore, the answer is"]]
