(which is 4, representing 40), and shift one position to the left:\n   \\[\n   36 \\times 40 = 1440\n   \\]\n   - Calculation: \\(6 \\times 4 = 24\\) (write down 4, carry over 2)\n   - \\(3 \\times 4 = 12 + 2 = 14\\) (write down 14, then add a zero)\n\n3. Add the results of the two steps:\n   \\[\n   324 + 1440 = 1764\n   \\]\n\nVerification using the distributive property:\n\\[\n36 \\times 49 = 36 \\times (50 - 1) = 36 \\times 50 - 36 \\times 1 = 1800 - 36 = 1764\n\\]\n\nAnother verification by expanding both numbers:\n\\[\n(30 + 6)(40 + 9) = 30 \\times 40 + 30 \\times 9 + 6 \\times 40 + 6 \\times 9 = 1200 + 270 + 240 + 54 = 1764\n\\]\n\nThus, the final computed product is \\(\\boxed{1764}\\).", '']
