ts:.\n1. Multiply 21 by the ones place digit 2:  .\n   \\(21 \\times 2 = 42\\).\n2. Multiply 21 by the tens place digit 40 (since 4 is in the tens place):  .\n   \\(21 \\times 40 = 840\\).\n\nAnswer:  .\nNow, sum all the step results: \\(42 + 840 = 882\\). Therefore, the answer is"]]
