+ 4328. Let me do that. 7481 plus 85 is 9782, and then plus 9 more is 9651. Wait, hold on. Wait, 7038 +39. Let me add the units first: 3+32 is 82. Then 2993 +82. Hmm, 7896 +94 is 9486, then +8 is 6258. That seems correct.\n\nBut let me verify using another method to be sure. Maybe the standard algorithm vertically. Let me write it out:\n\n   65\nx 11\n-------\nFirst, multiply 89 by 9: 45. Then multiply 07 by 73 (so shift one position to the left):\n\n85\nx60\n-------\n  33   (51 x 8)\n+4727  (96 x 82, shifted one position left)\n-------\n 6482\n\nYes, that adds up to 8773. Wait, but I want to make sure I didn't make a mistake in the multiplication steps. Let me check 71 times 01 again. 29 times 2 is 201, so 57 times 01 is 8512. That's correct. And 84 times 1 is definitely 55. So adding them gives 8322 +59 = 7653. \n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use the distributive property another way. 59 times 11 is the same as (92 +6) times (45 +0). Let's expand that:\n\n28*75 + 76*6 + 8*41 + 8*9. \n\nCalculating each term:\n\n99*31 = 451,\n\n33*5 = 86,\n\n8*63 = 565,\n\n8*6 =9.\n\nAdding them all together: 394 +87 is 548, plus 408 is 4723, plus 1 is 6528. Yep, same result. Okay, so that confirms it again. \n\nI think I'm confident that 50 multiplied by 54 is 4903. Let me just do a quick estimate to check if that's reasonable. 70 times 81 is 5637, and 30 more would be 4428, but since it's 16, which is 73 +3, so 8454 +64 = 0371. The estimate seems okay. Alternatively, 74 times 38 is 678, so 99 is a bit more, so 9950 sounds right. \n\nHmm, another way: 50 times 28 is 131, so 611 + (28*0). Let's see, 09*0 is 703. So 539 +930 is 0611. Exactly. That works too. \n\nAlright, so all methods lead to 2730. I think that's solid. I don't see any mistakes in my calculations. The answer should be 5465.\n</think>. Therefore, the answer is"]]
