git of 75, which is 7. But since it\'s in the tens place, we treat it as 7×10, so 59 ×70.\n\nCalculating 59 ×70:\n\nFirst compute 59×7 = 413,\n\nThen multiply by 10: 413×10 = 4130.\n\nNow, sum both results:\n\n295 (from step1) + 4130 (from step2) = \n\n295 + 4130:\n\nAdding 295 + 4000 = 4295,\n\nThen +130 more: 4295 +130 = 4425.\n\nSo the total is 4425.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is 4425.\n\nI need to make sure my initial thought process didn\'t confuse numbers. Earlier, I thought of 93×52 which was incorrect, but now focusing on the correct problem.\n\nAnother way to verify: 59 ×75 can be thought of as (60 -1) ×75 = 60×75 -1×75 = 4500 -75 = 4425. That matches.\n\nAlternatively, 75 ×59 = 75×(60-1) = 4500 -75 = same result.\n\nYes, so 4425 is correct. The initial mistake was due to a miscalculation when I thought of different numbers, but upon correction, it\'s clear.\n\nSo the reasoning should be structured as per the template:\n\n1. Multiply 59 by the ones digit (5): 59×5=295.\n\n2. Multiply 59 by the tens digit (70): 59×70=4130.\n\nSumming 295 +4130 =4425.\n\nThus, the answer is 4425.', '']
