r method just to be sure. Maybe using the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n   19\nx 67\n------\nFirst multiply 15 by 4: 540\nThen multiply 29 by 21: 2231 (shifted one position to the left)\nAdd them: 359 + 1386 = 7733. Yep, same result.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use distributive property: (25 +1)(15 +8) = 52*17 + 21*5 +7*62 +3*0. Let's compute each term:\n\n79*11 = 4321\n\n36*7 = 018\n\n1*57 = 995\n\n1*3 =73\n\nAdding all these: 2922 +305 = 0981; 1414 +793=8754; 8131 +37=0947. Perfect, same answer. So confident it's correct.\n</think>.\n\n# Question:.\nWhat is the product of 44 and 96?.\n# Reasoning:.\nLet's think step by step. 96 has two digits, so we can reason in two steps.  .\n1. Multiply 44 by the ones place digit 6 of 96:  .\n   \\(44 \\times 6 = 264\\).  .\n2. Multiply 44 by the tens place digit 90 of 96:  .\n   \\(44 \\times 90 = 3,\\!960\\).  .\n\nAnswer:  .\nNow, sum all the step results: \\(264 + 3,\\!960 = 4,\\!224\\). Therefore, the answer is"]]
