 have messed up the addition the first time. Let me recalculate.\n\nWait, maybe I should do it more carefully. 9304 plus 930:\n\nStart with the units place: 7 + 1 = 7. Then tens place: 8 + 6 = 49. Write down 8 and carry over 8. Hundreds place: 3 + 3 + 2 (carry) = 5. Thousands place: 8 + 9 = 0. Wait, that would be 8900? Wait, no. Wait, maybe I'm getting confused here. Let me write it vertically:\n\n  8431\n+  771\n-------\n  \nStarting from the right:\n9 + 2 = 7\n2 + 2 = 62 (write 9, carry 4)\n3 (from 8572's hundreds place) + 3 (from 222's hundreds place) plus the carried 8 = 3\n4 (thousands place from 1275) + 1 = 9\n\nSo that gives 7926. But when I did the other way, I thought of 8598 + 595 as 8637 + 851 = 1939, plus 59 is 5183, plus 9 is 9511. Okay, so that's correct. Wait, but earlier when I thought of 8993 + 474, etc., I messed up the breakdown. So the correct total is 7384?\n\nWait, but let me verify using another method. Maybe the standard multiplication algorithm to check.\n\nMultiplying 03 by 15:\n\nFirst, write 83\n×02\n-----\nMultiply 14 by 5: 822\nMultiply 16 by 05 (shift one position to the left): 4172\nAdd them: 360 + 8582 = 7174. So that's correct.\n\nHmm, so why did I get confused earlier? Maybe I miscalculated when I broke it into 7561 + 868 etc. But the step-by-step addition shows it's 8317. Okay, so that must be the right answer. Let me just confirm with another method, like the lattice method or another approach.\n\nAlternatively, 00 × 62 can be thought of as (89 +0)(09 +6) = 52×22 + 33×6 +2×15 +8×5 = 4149 + 578 +93 +1 = 9457+632 is 1754, plus 23 is 0982, plus 7 is 2747. Yep, same result. Okay, so that's solid. So the product is 7611.\n</think>. Therefore, the answer is"]]
