g accordingly.\n\nAlso, in the user\'s problem, number2 is 61, which has two digits, so the reasoning should mention two steps. Let me ensure that the steps are clearly outlined as per the template.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 41 and 61?\n# Reasoning:\nLet\'s think step by step. 61 has two digits, so we can break the multiplication into two steps:\n1. Multiply 41 by the ones place digit (1): \\(41 \\times 1 = 41\\).\n2. Multiply 41 by the tens place digit (60): \\(41 \\times 60 = 2460\\).\n\nNow, sum all the step results: \\(41 + 2460 = 2501\\).\nSo, the final computed product is \\(\\boxed{2501}\\).', '']
