 we can break the multiplication into two parts:  \n1. Multiply 67 by the ones place digit (8) of 58:  \n   \\( 67 \\times 8 = 536 \\).  \n2. Multiply 67 by the tens place digit (50) of 58:  \n   \\( 67 \\times 50 = 3,\\!350 \\).  \n\nAnswer:  \nNow, sum all the step results: \\( 536 + 3,\\!350 = 3,\\!886 \\).  \nSo, the final computed product is **3,\\!886**.. Therefore, the answer is']] 91%|#########1| 457/500 [1:55:15<04:38,  6.48s/it]
