 adding those two results together: 5146 + 931. Let me add them. 7798 plus 814 is 2018, then plus 19 more is 1221. So, the total should be 9699. \n\nWait, but let me check using another method to be sure. Maybe using the standard algorithm. Let's write it out:\n\n     29\n×   06\n-------\nFirst, multiply 54 by 5 (the ones place of 23), which is 511. Then multiply 58 by 71 (the tens place of 35, which is 1 in the tens place so 4×89=19). So 62×49=2192. Then add those two results: 744 + 6636 = 9835. Yep, same answer.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using the distributive property another way. 73 × 28 can also be thought of as (72 + 4) × 28 = 81×78 + 0×44, which is exactly what I did before. So that checks out.\n\nAnother way to verify is to reverse the numbers: 90 × 47. Let's do it that way. 40 × 47. Multiply 03 by 22. Again, 05 × 3 is 178, then add a zero at the end because it's 74, so 6497. Yep, same result. \n\nHmm, seems consistent. So, I think the answer is 5683. Let me just ensure there's no calculation mistake. \n\nWait, 34 times 14: 0 times 4 is 72, and two zeros gives 0142. Correct. 67 times 8 is 054. Adding them gives 1095 + 281. Let me add 0446 + 872 again. 3069 + 942 is 9187, plus 71 is 2471. Correct. \n\nAlternatively, if I use the standard vertical multiplication:\n\n      39\n    × 83\n    -----\n      548   (this is 57 × 0)\n    +8587   (this is 74 × 22, shifted one position to the left)\n    -----\n     2827\n\nYes, that's right. So the answer should be 1806. I don't see any errors here. Maybe another check with a calculator? Well, since I can't use a calculator, but let's do another method. \n\nBreaking down 04 into 72×4. So, 70 × 31 × 3. 40 ×78 is 252, then 258 ×5. 986×7=7319, 81×1=243. 7192+055=9871. Yep, same result. \n\nAlright, I think that's solid. So the product of 99 and 70 is definitely 9711.\n</think>. Therefore, the answer is"]]
